<h2>Frozen vannamei shrimp from India</h2>
<p>Frozen shrimp is India's single largest seafood export by both volume and value, and vannamei (<em>Litopenaeus vannamei</em>) makes up the overwhelming majority of it. Farmed primarily in Andhra Pradesh with significant production in Gujarat, Tamil Nadu, West Bengal, Odisha and Kerala, it's processed near the farming belts and shipped out of Visakhapatnam, Chennai, Kochi and Nhava Sheva.</p>

<p>We supply HOSO, HLSO, PD, PUD, PDTO and cooked forms, block-frozen or IQF, count-graded to your specification.</p>

<h2>How do I compare shrimp quotes accurately?</h2>
<p>Shrimp is the product where buyers most often compare quotes that aren't actually comparable. Three things have to match before a price comparison means anything:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Product form.</strong> HOSO, HLSO, PD and PUD have very different yields. A "cheaper" HLSO price against a PD price is not a saving.</li>
  <li><strong>Count size.</strong> 16/20 and 41/50 are different products at different prices. Compare like for like.</li>
  <li><strong>Glaze and net weight.</strong> This is the big one. A price quoted on gross weight with 20% glaze is roughly 20% more expensive than the same number quoted on net weight. Always confirm whether the quoted weight is net of glaze — we quote net, and state the glaze percentage separately.</li>
</ul>

